From ca19d740b48d26dd2b88ff0b240c0deedfaf230e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:36:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/58] feat: opt-in lemond LAN beacon listener, list-only

Add a beacon_listen config key (default false). When enabled, lemond binds
UDP 13305 on each local RFC1918 interface's directed-broadcast address plus
255.255.255.255 (never INADDR_ANY, so 127.0.0.1 CLI/Tauri discovery is
untouched), validates heard beacons (RFC1918 source, strict URL bound to the
source IP, sanitised hostname, self filter, two-tier rate limit, 32-row cap,
15 s TTL) and reports them as beacon_listener in GET /health. Heard hosts are
display-only: nothing contacts them or registers them as providers. Windows
builds a stub that reports supported=false.

The broadcaster now builds its payload with nlohmann::json (replace on
invalid UTF-8, try/catch around each send) and adds an instance_id for
exact self-detection.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
